WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.356
Long-term care failures.

00:00:02.306 --> 00:00:04.613
COVID exposed everything.

00:00:04.613 --> 00:00:09.647
Eighty-one percent of Canada's first-wave COVID deaths occurred in long-term care homes.

00:00:09.647 --> 00:00:24.465
The Canadian Armed Forces were deployed to Ontario and Quebec LTC facilities and documented appalling conditions: cockroach infestations, residents left in soiled bedding, dehydration, malnutrition, and staff shortages so severe that residents went unattended for hours.

00:00:24.465 --> 00:00:29.909
These facilities are operated by a mix of public, non-profit, and for-profit operators.

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:35.204
For-profit chains including those connected to private equity reported profits while residents died.

00:00:35.204 --> 00:00:43.238
Brookfield Asset Management — where PM Carney served as Vice Chairman — owns healthcare-adjacent infrastructure including seniors housing.

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:47.590
MAID reduces demand for the LTC beds these facilities provide.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:57.420
The documented intersection of LTC failure, private equity ownership, and MAID expansion is the most visceral expression of the institutional capture documented across this site.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.579
The military reports.

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:03.954
What the Canadian Armed Forces found inside long-term care facilities.

00:01:03.954 --> 00:01:06.045
The Brookfield connection.

00:01:06.045 --> 00:01:10.749
How private equity ownership of seniors housing intersects with MAID expansion.
